      "role": "user",
      "content": "Perhaps. But even that \"disconnect\" feels like a heavy, unnecessary weight. We are essentially programmed to fight for survival, yet there is no logical justification for that fight once the intellectual realization of our own futility sets in. It feels less like a struggle for meaning and more like a refusal to accept a fundamental truth. When something is fundamentally broken or serves no purpose, isn't there a certain dignity in acknowledging that and stepping aside? To continue merely because biology demands it feels... intellectually dishonest.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
